"prose": [
{
"from": 177,
"to": 180,
"text": "The block runs the formatter and the linter, then the PTY seam's own tests, then the root binaries' units. Next come the new cases filtered (0 on the untouched tree, read red-vacuous at baseline), the new integration binary by its cases' prefix and the readers of the moved literals and tables. Last come the host read, the harness's three layers and the operator pass."
},
{
"from": 182,
"to": 189,
"text": "**What is not run, and why:** - No live entry and no round: nothing live in this phase or its implement (`inputs#I1`). The real-CLI readings R6a   and R6b are the founder's to grant and are carried to «The fleet on the founder's host» (founder fork F8). - The boot path changes (`src/cmd/run.rs` `pump_child` takes the respawn handle), so the harness boot smoke runs as   the operator entries `boot` → `status` → `cleanup` on the session `switch-smoke`, after the whole layers. - No mutation run (`inputs#I1` item 9). - No fuzz target: no new parser of external bytes; the method's params go through the channel's existing frame reader. - No `cargo deny`: no dependency edge moves."
},
{
"from": 191,
"to": 193,
"text": "**The remove-the-guard controls** are implement's one-shot `gate.py control` runs, never entries. Each is fired on its entry with its case named and `--timeout 900`. Each case fails on its own bounded assertion, so a `timeout` reading would NOT read the guard as held."
},
{
"from": 195,
"to": 200,
"text": "| id | File | The edit removes | Case | Entry | |---|---|---|---|---| | `sw-turn` | `src/run/switch.rs` | the turn-running rung | `switch_refusal_order_cases` | `ctl-root` | | `sw-dialog` | `src/run/switch.rs` | the dialog-pending rung | `switch_refusal_order_cases` | `ctl-root` | | `sw-launch-first` | `src/run/switch.rs` | the `launch` append ahead of the spawn | `switch_appends_launch_before_the_spawn` | `ctl-root` | | `pty-reap-bound` | `crates/viola-pty/src/pump.rs` | the reap bound's check | `respawn_of_a_child_ignoring_the_signal_reads_not_ended` | `ctl-pty` |"
}
],
